{
    "readme": "Reference configuration for remotely-configured event-driven metrics. Metrics are declared in the settings of the experiment subfeatures they measure: content scope experiments and TDS experiments. Each key under settings.metrics is a metric name; its value carries the event that converts it and one or more {windows, thresholds} conversion groups whose product defines how it converts. searchLike demonstrates the partial product production retention metrics use - threshold 1 over per-day windows in one group, higher thresholds over range windows in another. Metric names are scoped to their experiment: captchaSeen and pageLoad appear in several experiments bound to the same event and convert together, while contentScopeExperiment21 binds captchaSeen to a different event entirely and must convert independently - a name means nothing outside its experiment. The TDS experiment parent feature is blockList on Android and contentBlocking elsewhere, so this fixture carries identical TDS experiment definitions under both names; a client must read exactly the parent it ships against, never both. There is no state field on a metric: presence means it converts. Cohort weights are irrelevant here because tests declare enrolled experiments directly via activeExperiments; cohort assignment and enrollment are owned by each experiment type and are out of scope.",
